IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sss-act`
IMPORT `sss-administration`

-- Silver Support Scheme Act 2015, ss 8, 9 and 13 to 19 -- worked cases.

§ `8 -- compelled disclosure between departments`

GIVEN `kind` IS AN InformationKind, `certified` IS A BOOLEAN, `necessary only` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN, `information recipient` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DisclosureDirection
DECIDE `a direction` `kind` `certified` `necessary only` `authorised person` `information recipient` IS
    DisclosureDirection WITH
        `the kind` IS `kind`
        `the Minister certified in writing that access is necessary` IS `certified`
        `the purpose is the administration or enforcement of this Act or the administration of the Scheme` IS TRUE
        `the responsible Minister directed the department or public authority` IS TRUE
        `no more than is necessary for that purpose was directed to be provided` IS `necessary only`
        `the recipient is an authorised person` IS `authorised person`
        `the recipient is an information recipient` IS `information recipient`

#ASSERT `the direction is validly given` (`a direction` `means information` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- No written certificate of necessity, no valid direction.
#ASSERT NOT `the direction is validly given` (`a direction` `means information` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- More than is necessary, no valid direction.
#ASSERT NOT `the direction is validly given` (`a direction` `means information` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)

-- The recipient must match the subsection: means information goes to an
-- AUTHORISED PERSON, other confidential information to an INFORMATION
-- RECIPIENT. Crossing them over fails.
#ASSERT NOT `the direction is validly given` (`a direction` `means information` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the direction is validly given` (`a direction` `confidential information other than means information` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the direction is validly given` (`a direction` `confidential information other than means information` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)

-- "DESPITE ANY OTHER WRITTEN LAW, AND WHETHER OR NOT IT IS UNDER ANY OBLIGATION
-- ... NOT TO DISCLOSE": an existing duty of confidence is no answer. The pair
-- on that fact is the point -- the answer does not move.
#ASSERT `the department must comply with the direction` (`a direction` `means information` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) TRUE
#ASSERT `the department must comply with the direction` (`a direction` `means information` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) FALSE
-- But an invalid direction compels nothing.
#ASSERT NOT `the department must comply with the direction` (`a direction` `means information` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE) FALSE

§ `9 -- what may then be done with it`

-- s 9(2): a closed purpose test, or consent.
#ASSERT `the use or disclosure is authorised by section 9(2)` `the administration of the Scheme` FALSE
#ASSERT `the use or disclosure is authorised by section 9(2)` `the administration or enforcement of this Act` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the use or disclosure is authorised by section 9(2)` `some other purpose` FALSE
#ASSERT `the use or disclosure is authorised by section 9(2)` `some other purpose` TRUE

GIVEN `derived` IS A BOOLEAN, `prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN, `requested` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `approved` IS A BOOLEAN, `right form` IS A BOOLEAN, `opted out` IS A BOOLEAN, `consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN OnwardReport
DECIDE `a report` `derived` `prescribed` `requested` `approved` `right form` `opted out` `consented` IS
    OnwardReport WITH
        `the information is derived from information obtained under section 8` IS `derived`
        `the receiving scheme is prescribed for the purposes of section 9(3)` IS `prescribed`
        `it was requested by the recipient` IS `requested`
        `the Minister approved` IS `approved`
        `it is in the form of a report stating only the two matters in section 9(3)(b)` IS `right form`
        `the individual has opted out and the Commissioner, Board or administrator has been notified` IS `opted out`
        `the individual consented despite having opted out` IS `consented`

#ASSERT `the report may lawfully be provided` (`a report` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)

-- Every one of the five s 9(3) conditions is necessary.
#ASSERT NOT `the report may lawfully be provided` (`a report` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the report may lawfully be provided` (`a report` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the report may lawfully be provided` (`a report` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the report may lawfully be provided` (`a report` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the report may lawfully be provided` (`a report` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- s 9(5): the opt-out stops the report, and only the individual's consent
-- restores it. IT IS AN OPT-OUT, NOT AN OPT-IN -- the reports flow unless the
-- person finds out they can stop them.
#ASSERT `section 9(5) forbids providing the report` (`a report` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the report may lawfully be provided` (`a report` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the report may lawfully be provided` (`a report` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)

§ `13 -- the administrator's certificate`

#ASSERT `the certificate is prima facie evidence of the amount` `the amount of benefit received as at a date` TRUE
#ASSERT `the certificate is prima facie evidence of the amount` `the amount recoverable as at a date` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the certificate is prima facie evidence of the amount` `something else` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the certificate is prima facie evidence of the amount` `the amount recoverable as at a date` FALSE

§ `14 and 15 -- the information powers, and obstruction`

GIVEN `required` IS A BOOLEAN, `provided` IS A BOOLEAN, `excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN InformationRequirement
DECIDE `a requirement` `required` `provided` `excuse` IS
    InformationRequirement WITH
        `the Commissioner or an investigator required information or a document under section 14(1)(b)` IS `required`
        `the person provided it within the time allowed` IS `provided`
        `the person had a reasonable excuse` IS `excuse`

#ASSERT `an offence under section 14(4) is committed` (`a requirement` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 14(4) is committed` (`a requirement` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- A reasonable excuse answers it.
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 14(4) is committed` (`a requirement` TRUE FALSE TRUE)

#ASSERT `an offence under section 15 is committed` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 15 is committed` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 15 is committed` FALSE FALSE

-- THE PENALTY RANKING. Obstructing an investigator carries the HIGHEST maximum
-- fine in the Act at $20,000. Failing to produce a document carries $10,000.
-- Misusing a recipient's private information carries $5,000 -- and so does
-- dishonestly obtaining a benefit under s 11.
#ASSERT `the maximum fine under section 15 in dollars` EQUALS 20000
#ASSERT `the maximum fine under section 14(4) in dollars` EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `the maximum fine under section 9(7) in dollars` EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `the maximum fine under section 11 in dollars` EQUALS 5000

§ `16 -- attribution to individuals`

GIVEN `kind` IS A BodyKind, `proved` IS A BOOLEAN, `connivance` IS A BOOLEAN, `neglect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN AttributionFacts
DECIDE `attribution` `kind` `proved` `connivance` `neglect` IS
    AttributionFacts WITH
        `the kind` IS `kind`
        `an offence under this Act by the body is proved` IS `proved`
        `committed with the consent or connivance of the individual` IS `connivance`
        `attributable to neglect on the individual's part` IS `neglect`

#ASSERT `the individual is also guilty of the offence` (`attribution` `a body corporate` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- NEGLECT ALONE IS ENOUGH. No consent, no connivance, no knowledge: mere
-- neglect makes the officer personally guilty of the body's offence.
#ASSERT `the individual is also guilty of the offence` (`attribution` `a body corporate` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the individual is also guilty of the offence` (`attribution` `a body corporate` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- No offence by the body, nothing to attribute.
#ASSERT NOT `the individual is also guilty of the offence` (`attribution` `a body corporate` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- The same two limbs reach partners and association officers.
#ASSERT `the individual is also guilty of the offence` (`attribution` `a partnership` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the individual is also guilty of the offence` (`attribution` `an unincorporated association other than a partnership` TRUE FALSE TRUE)

§ `17 -- composition, and its double ceiling`

-- "the LOWER of (a) one half of the maximum fine; (b) $1,000."
-- For the s 15 offence the half-limb is $10,000, so $1,000 governs.
#ASSERT `the composition ceiling` 20000 EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `the composition ceiling` 5000 EQUALS 1000
-- The half-limb could only bite on an offence with a maximum of $2,000 or less,
-- and the Act creates none. At $2,000 the two limbs meet exactly.
#ASSERT `the composition ceiling` 2000 EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `the composition ceiling` 1800 EQUALS 900

#ASSERT `the offence may be compounded for that sum` TRUE 20000 1000
#ASSERT NOT `the offence may be compounded for that sum` TRUE 20000 1001
#ASSERT NOT `the offence may be compounded for that sum` FALSE 20000 100

§ `19 -- protection from personal liability`

#ASSERT `no personal liability lies` `the Commissioner for Silver Support` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `no personal liability lies` `an investigator` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Good faith is not enough without reasonable care, and the converse.
#ASSERT NOT `no personal liability lies` `an investigator` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `no personal liability lies` `an investigator` FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- And only for the six classes s 19(1) names.
#ASSERT NOT `no personal liability lies` `someone outside the section 19(1) list` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- And only in the execution or purported execution of the Act.
#ASSERT NOT `no personal liability lies` `an investigator` TRUE TRUE FALSE
